# FoxESS Cloud Patterns

## Architecture

- `main.js` — single file; entire adapter logic (no `lib/` submodules)
- Class: `Foxesscloud extends utils.Adapter`
- No separate connector classes; API calls directly in adapter class

## API communication

- Base URL: `https://www.foxesscloud.com/`
- Auth headers: `token` (API key) + `signature` (MD5 hash) + `timestamp`
- **Critical:** signature uses **literal** `\r\n` strings (not real line breaks):

```javascript
const signatureString = `${path}\\r\\n${token}\\r\\n${milliseconds}`;
const signature = crypto.createHash('md5').update(signatureString).digest('hex');
```

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| POST | `/op/v1/device/real/query` | Real-time data — preferred; `{ sns[], variables[] }` (up to 50 SNs) |
| POST | `/op/v0/device/real/query` | Real-time data — deprecated; `{ sn, variables[] }` |
| POST | `/op/v0/device/list` | All inverters (paginated) |
| GET | `/op/v0/device/variable/get` | All variables with names and units |
| GET | `/op/v0/user/getAccessCount` | Rate limit (total + remaining) |

~50–65 real-time variables per inverter depending on model.

## Polling

- Start in `onReady()` via `this.setInterval()`; store handle in `this.updateInterval`
- Stop in `onUnload()` with `this.clearInterval(this.updateInterval)`
- Interval from config: `this.config.interval` (seconds, minimum 60)

## State naming

- Current: flat hierarchy under adapter instance (e.g. `foxesscloud.0.pvPower`)
- Planned (multi-device): device folder by serial number (e.g. `foxesscloud.0.<deviceSN>.pvPower`)
- Info state: `info.connection` (true = connected, false = error/disconnected)
- Variable names follow FoxESS API (camelCase): `pvPower`, `SoC`, `generationPower`, etc.

## Pitfalls

- Do not use axios or other HTTP libraries — stick to `node:https`
- Do not forget signature `\r\n` escaping
- Always clear poll interval in `onUnload`
- Respect API rate limits; check `getAccessCount` when debugging
